# K02c (next_core_tasks_v2.md K02, bullet 3; defects.md MERGE-HIDDEN-INPUT-PROJECTION; Codex, DS-CODEX-004): a merge
# result reaching a callee as an ORDINARY hidden input, the caller's binding first.  `copy` is a unit-level merge
# result (value 1); `read` names the free `copy\value`; `caller` declares its OWN `copy: merge: Other` (value 22) and
# calls read.  By the general priority of a free name's sources (the book §12: the caller's binding, an inherited
# input, the lexical fallback) read takes the caller's copy: 22, not the unit's 1.  Was 81: the unit's result-name
# lookup bypassed the dynamic input (l2_scan_ident's early return).  Success is 7.
Model: (int: value 1)
Other: (int: value 22)
copy: merge: Model
fn: read () int
return: copy\value
fn: caller () int
    copy: merge: Other
    return: read()
end: caller
int: result caller()
if: result != 22
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
